#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/be.rc -- Belarusian (Belarus), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "be"`.
//
// Stage E108, group A: the two string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the menu
// block -- in the order of en.rc. Left to right, Cyrillic script of the Belarusian alphabet (ў, і,
// the apostrophe '; no и, щ, ъ), the official orthography. The polite "вы" form addresses the
// reader, in the plural, so the reader's gender is not shown; the author speaks as a man (RULES 14).
// The preposition and the word "у" become "ў" after a vowel. Quotes are the guillemets «», as in
// the Russian text. The key names stay in Latin letters, as the hotkey field prints them (RULES 4).
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Belarusian — `[general] language = "be"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
